-- compute_intent_drift.spl
-- LLM-as-judge scoring for `grafcode drift --mode semantic` — despite the
-- filename (kept for compat; this predates semantic mode existing for any
-- dimension but `intent`), this now judges whichever of the 5 drift
-- dimensions (structural/interface/intent/behavior/implementation) the
-- caller names via @dimension, not just intent — see graph_lib.py's
-- drift_report() docstring for why "semantic" applies uniformly across all
-- five, each judging its own text representation of that dimension rather
-- than intent_text() specifically.
--
-- Why judge, not embedding distance: the schema doc's original spec for
-- `intent` was "embedding distance over defines/comment fields", but
-- `grafcode drift --llm` takes an ADAPTER:MODEL pair (e.g.
-- claude_cli:claude-sonnet-4-6) the same way `extract --llm` and
-- `compile_blueprint.spl` do — and claude_cli isn't an embeddings endpoint.
-- Rather than bolt on a separate, hardcoded embedding-API dependency this
-- project otherwise has none of, this asks the SAME model named by --llm to
-- judge dissimilarity directly (LLM-as-judge), the same GENERATE-based
-- pattern compile_blueprint.spl already uses to draft blueprints — judging
-- instead of drafting.
--
--   spl3 run spl/compute_intent_drift.spl --tools spl/tools.py \
--     -p dimension=interface \
--     -p intent_a="$(cat /tmp/text_a.txt)" \
--     -p intent_b="$(cat /tmp/text_b.txt)" \
--     -p output_path=/tmp/drift_score.txt \
--     --llm claude_cli:claude-sonnet-4-6
--
-- `grafcode drift --mode semantic --llm ...` is the normal caller — for
-- each selected dimension it builds @intent_a/@intent_b from that
-- dimension's own text representation (graph_lib.py's _DIM_TEXT_BUILDERS)
-- and reads @output_path back rather than parsing stdout, the same
-- file-based handoff `extract --llm` uses for its blueprint YAML output.

CREATE FUNCTION judge_intent_drift(dimension TEXT, intent_a TEXT, intent_b TEXT)
RETURN TEXT
AS $$
You are scoring how much the "{dimension}" aspect has drifted between two
versions of the same blueprint graph. Judge only what "{dimension}" means in
this schema — structural is node/edge topology, interface is exported call
signatures, behavior is verification checks, implementation is the
tech-stack primitive set, intent is human-readable rationale (why a node
exists, not what it does). Do not penalize differences that belong to a
different dimension than the one named above.

Version A's {dimension} text:
{intent_a}

Version B's {dimension} text:
{intent_b}

Score how much this dimension has changed, as a continuous value:
- 0.00 = unchanged in substance, even if the wording/formatting differs
  entirely (a faithful paraphrase or reordering is 0.00, not a partial
  score — you are scoring substantive drift, not text similarity)
- 1.00 = completely different, contradictory, or unrelated
- An entry (node, signature, check, etc.) present in one version and
  missing from the other counts toward drift, weighted by roughly how much
  of each version's total content it represents (losing one entry out of
  twenty is a small score; losing the only entry is close to 1.00)

CRITICAL: output ONLY a single number between 0.00 and 1.00 — nothing else.
No explanation, no units, no surrounding text, no markdown. Valid outputs
look exactly like: 0.00 | 0.15 | 0.5 | 1.00
$$

WORKFLOW compute_intent_drift
    INPUT:
        @dimension TEXT DEFAULT 'intent',
        @intent_a TEXT DEFAULT '',
        @intent_b TEXT DEFAULT '',
        @output_path TEXT DEFAULT 'logs/spl/intent_drift_score.txt',
        @log_dir TEXT DEFAULT 'logs/spl'
    OUTPUT:
        @result TEXT
DO
    CALL now_float() INTO @t_start
    GENERATE judge_intent_drift(@dimension, @intent_a, @intent_b) INTO @score_text
    CALL write_file(@output_path, @score_text, "w") INTO @path
    CALL time_elapsed(@t_start) INTO @elapsed
    LOGGING f"{@dimension} drift score: {@score_text} ({@elapsed}s) -> {@path}" LEVEL INFO
    RETURN @score_text
END
